And-indeed I-wept over the-scattering-of our-union, * a-measure (that) made-overflow the-tears from my-eyelids;
and-I-vowed, if returned the-time (to) gather-us, * not I-return I-mention a-parting with-my-tongue.
Rushed the-joy upon-me until that-I, * from the-greatness-of what indeed gladdened-me, it-made-me-weep.
